1	// {init, transition} adapter over a v2 SAM strict-profile spec module — the
2	// ONLY way into check.mjs's BFS engine. The transition relation is derived
3	// mechanically from the module here; it is never hand-authored and is not an
4	// artifact contract. (It was, once: the 1.x `next(state, action, data)`
5	// module. That surface is gone — see CHANGELOG 8.0.0.)
6	//
7	// Adapted from SysMoBench's tools/js-sam/lean-adapter.cjs (verified unmodified
8	// against v2 in E2-v2), with two deliberate differences:
9	//   - factory form: makeSamAdapter(specModule) wraps an ALREADY-LOADED module
10	//     (the pipeline loads specs through load-spec.mjs, which pins the SAM
11	//     library to the vendored 2.0.0-alpha bundle) instead of the env-var +
12	//     require() selection the SysMoBench explorer needed;
13	//   - rejection detection reads instance({}).lastStep().classification
14	//     ('rejected' — the v2 strict-profile signal) first, keeping the v1
15	//     error-slot 'unexpected action' prefix as a compatibility fallback.
16	//
17	// Semantics:
18	//   init()                -> spec.init(); return sanitized spec.getState()
19	//   step(state, i, data)  -> spec.init() (reset); clear error slot;
20	//                           spec.setState(state); spec.actions[i](data);
21	//                           returns { state, verdict, reason }:
22	//                             verdict 'rejected' — the acceptor rejected; state
23	//                               is the INPUT state (a rejection is a legal,
24	//                               observable no-op, not a fault) and reason is
25	//                               the acceptor's reject(reason), when readable.
26	//                             verdict 'accepted' — state is the post snapshot.
27	//                           Any other model-error content or strict-profile
28	//                           throw propagates, so the checker records it as a
29	//                           violation. step() is the full-fidelity surface:
